          "distinct": false,
          "id": "93091573a5b5dac7b47379f55cce5feb0070c413",
          "message": "gui: strip the legacy noModule polyfills chunk from the Tauri-target export (sq-zv37m) (#2016)\n\n* gui: strip the legacy noModule polyfills chunk from the Tauri-target export (sq-zv37m) [FABLE-5]\n\nNext.js static export unconditionally emits a ~110 KB (112,594 B raw / 39,509 B\ngz) polyfills-*.js chunk referenced only via <script noModule> tags. The Tauri 2\nwebview is always ES-module-capable, so it never fetches the chunk — pure dead\ninstaller weight. Add a post-export strip wired into `build:tauri` ONLY\n(`build:web` / the hosted /app deploy are untouched): delete the chunk, remove\nits noModule tags, then hard-error if any `polyfills-` reference survives or if\nNext stops emitting the chunk (so the step is removed rather than rotting once\nthe proposed upstream config seam lands). 3 unit tests (mutation-checked).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* research: prepared upstream Next.js seam to omit the noModule polyfills chunk (sq-zv37m) [FABLE-5]\n\nDesign record for the vercel/next.js draft patch (NOT yet proposed upstream):\nexperimental.legacyBrowserPolyfills: false skips the CopyFilePlugin that emits\npolyfills-*.js, emptying buildManifest.polyfillFiles and omitting the noModule\ntag in both routers. Includes injection map, full diff (+82/-0, mirrors the\nfallbackNodePolyfills convention), prior art (#86785/#88551/#87270/#75820),\nand open questions for @jeswr to review before anything goes to the Next.js\nmaintainers (upstream-contribution protocol).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-12T02:06:43Z",
