          "id": "23c5888eb06eed0e342e900cb4b92b3f9fa13b24",
          "message": "test(sparq-acbench): behavioral oracle kill-assertions — compile_*∘oracle_* fail-closed (sq-3bv7v) [FABLE-5] (#2028)\n\nNew tests/oracle_behavioral.rs (test-only diff, no new deps): per-model\nbehavioral assertions that kill effect/condition-ignoring mutants across\nWAC/ACP/ODRL — fail-closed on no-match over a NON-empty intent table\n(wrong agent/resource/mode), Deny-effect anti-vacuity through both the\ncompiler polarity (acp:deny / odrl:prohibition, never the allow\npredicate) and the oracle decision, ODRL permission-overrides-prohibition\nprecedence pinned, and condition gating flipping Allow⇄Deny (Count,\ntemporal vs the pinned instant, compound And; WAC/ACP skip conditioned\nrows + compile Unsupported).\n\nMutation-witnessed: oracle_acp→always-Allow, Count(0)→satisfied,\nWAC deny-guard drop, and compile_odrl deny→permission each turn the\nsuite red.\n\nBead: sq-3bv7v (epic sq-3dyje mutation-honesty)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
